    "UniqueConceptKey": "F-267-anonymous-hotline-net-benefit",
    "Stem": "Maya Caldwell, treasurer at Flash Capital, is evaluating a confidential anonymous whistleblower hotline. Flash Capital's internal control testing shows that existing controls detect and recover 25% of the $2,000,000 expected annual fraud loss in its trading division. Industry benchmarks indicate an independently administered anonymous hotline would raise the detection rate to 60%. The hotline would cost $100,000 per year to operate. Which option best evaluates the net annual benefit of implementing the hotline?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "$700,000, the reduction in expected undetected fraud loss before operating costs",
      "B": "$800,000, the expected annual undetected fraud loss remaining after the hotline is implemented",
      "C": "$1,500,000, the expected annual undetected fraud loss before the hotline is implemented",
      "D": "$600,000, the reduction in expected undetected fraud loss net of the $100,000 annual operating cost"
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "D",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "Before the hotline, undetected fraud loss = $2,000,000 x (1 - 0.25) = $1,500,000. After the hotline, undetected loss = $2,000,000 x (1 - 0.60) = $800,000. The reduction is $1,500,000 - $800,000 = $700,000, and netting the $100,000 operating cost yields $700,000 - $100,000 = $600,000 net annual benefit. Recomputed: 2,000,000 x 0.75 = 1,500,000; 2,000,000 x 0.40 = 800,000; 1,500,000 - 800,000 - 100,000 = 600,000. SOX Section 806 and the IMA resolution process support confidential whistleblower channels as a governance mechanism for fraud detection.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "$700,000 is the gross reduction in expected undetected loss ($1,500,000 - $800,000) but omits the $100,000 annual operating cost of the hotline. The question asks for net annual benefit, so the operating cost must be deducted, giving $600,000.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "$800,000 is the expected undetected fraud loss remaining after implementation ($2,000,000 x 0.40), not the net benefit. This figure answers a different question - the residual exposure - rather than the annual benefit of the hotline.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "$1,500,000 is the pre-implementation expected undetected loss ($2,000,000 x 0.75). It describes the problem the hotline addresses, not the benefit produced, and ignores both the new detection rate and the operating cost.",
