    "UniqueConceptKey": "affiliate-transfer-pricing-objectivity",
    "Stem": "Priya Ramaswamy, senior analyst at Flash Holdings, prepares segment reporting for Flash Logistics and Flash Foods, which transact at a historical internal transfer rate. The CFO, Adaeze Onuorah, asks Priya to record a lower market-based transfer price for the period so Flash Foods reports higher margins, even though the services were actually billed at the historical rate. Under the IMA Objectivity Standard, what should Priya do?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Decline to restate the period's transfer price unless it reflects the actual terms of the transaction, and disclose the transfer-pricing basis in the segment notes.",
      "B": "Make the change because internal transfer pricing is a matter of management judgment.",
      "C": "Make the change but disclose it only to Adaeze in a private memo.",
      "D": "Refuse the change and immediately report Adaeze's instruction to the external auditors, bypassing the internal escalation process."
    },
