    "UniqueConceptKey": "ethics-hotline-retaliation-investigation-outcome",
    "Stem": "Naomi Castellanos, a project manager at Flash Industrial, filed an ethics hotline report questioning how certain project costs were capitalized. The internal investigation concluded that the report was made in good faith but found no evidence of misconduct. Adaeze Onuorah, the CFO, must now decide how to handle the outcome. Under the IMA Statement of Ethical Professional Practice and Flash Industrial's ethics program, what is the appropriate course of action?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Reprimand Naomi so that future hotline reports are more carefully considered before filing.",
      "B": "Reassign Naomi to a less visible project to limit disruption while the matter is being closed.",
      "C": "Close the matter with no adverse action against Naomi, who reported in good faith.",
      "D": "Require Naomi to issue a written retraction to the employees named in her report."
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "C",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "A good-faith reporter of suspected misconduct is protected from retaliation even when the investigation does not substantiate the allegations, so Naomi should face no adverse action once the matter is closed.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "Disciplining Naomi for a report made in good faith is retaliation and would deter employees from using the hotline, even though the investigation did not find evidence supporting her allegations.",
