    "Stem": "Mariela Hoffmann, controller of Flash Manufacturing, prepares the company's forecast for the coming year. Projected revenue of $50.0 million assumes a key customer will renew a five-year supply contract; without renewal, revenue would be $45.0 million, and incremental revenue carries a 60% contribution margin. The forecast is distributed to the board and lenders without any mention of the renewal assumption. By how much is projected operating income overstated by the omitted assumption?",
