    "ExplanationWrongC": "The FCPA prohibits corrupt payments made indirectly as well as directly, including gifts routed through family members or agents, so directing the gift to the official's family does not remove it from the statute's reach.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Recording the gift as a marketing expense does not cure an FCPA violation, because the statute's anti-bribery and books-and-records provisions prohibit both the corrupt payment itself and its mischaracterization in the company's accounts.",
