    "QuestionID": "P2-F-301",
    "question_state": "Certified",
    "Part2OnlyFlag": true,
    "UniqueConceptKey": "confidentiality-proprietary-code-containment-duty",
    "Stem": "Mariela Hoffmann, controller of Flash Industrial, learns that a former systems engineer now employed by a competitor posted sections of Flash's proprietary route-optimization algorithm on a public developer forum. Legal counsel advises that the posting likely breaches the engineer's confidentiality agreement, and no statute requires Flash to act. A board member asks Mariela to 'handle it quietly' to avoid publicity. Under the IMA Statement of Ethical Professional Practice, which action best satisfies Mariela's confidentiality responsibilities?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Advise the board member that the leak is an employment matter outside the finance function and take no further action.",
      "B": "Treat the matter as a private dispute with the engineer and await the competitor's response before informing anyone inside Flash.",
      "C": "Withhold the information from internal audit until the engineer's former manager confirms the code is genuinely proprietary.",
      "D": "Inform the appropriate internal parties of the misuse and take reasonable steps to limit further dissemination of the code."
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "D",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "The confidentiality standard requires Mariela to keep information confidential except where disclosure is authorized or legally required, to inform relevant parties of its appropriate use, and to monitor compliance; informing the appropriate internal parties and containing further dissemination of the leaked code satisfies that duty where silence would compound the breach.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "Confidentiality obligations are not limited to documents the finance function itself prepared; once Mariela possesses confidential information about Flash Industrial, the standard obliges her to inform relevant parties of its misuse, so declaring the leak outside her scope and taking no further action permits the breach to continue.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Waiting for the competitor to respond turns a known misuse of Flash's confidential information into a passive waiting game; the confidentiality standard requires affirmative steps to inform the relevant internal parties and prevent further dissemination rather than deferring action to an outside party whose response may never come.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "The confidentiality standard does not condition disclosure on an internal verification of ownership; delaying notification to internal audit while the code remains exposed lets the misuse persist, and Mariela's duty to inform relevant parties of inappropriate use operates regardless of what the engineer's former manager later confirms.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "",
