    "ExplanationWrongA": "Direct SEC contact before the company self-reports is not a prerequisite; the internal-reporting alternative under the SEC whistleblower rules can preserve eligibility when the company reports the information within 120 days and the whistleblower files the required submission with the SEC within the prescribed deadline, so Lena is not categorically ineligible.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Rewards are not automatic: the SEC must obtain monetary sanctions above the statutory threshold and the whistleblower must submit the required information to the SEC within the filing deadline; an internal report that merely precipitates a company self-report does not by itself guarantee an award.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Retaliation protection under SOX §806 is a separate remedy from reward eligibility; demonstrating retaliation supports a whistleblower's own claims for relief but is not a condition for receiving an award, whose criteria turn on original information, a successful action, and timely SEC submissions.",
