      "rule_or_proposition": "The FCPA prohibits corruptly offering anything of value to a foreign official to obtain or retain business, but permits reasonable and bona fide expenditures directly related to promotion, demonstration, or contract performance and modest customary hospitality.",
      "application_to_facts": "The $40 pen set is customary business hospitality, while the all-expenses-paid family resort vacation is a lavish personal benefit given to influence the award of the foreign government contract.",
      "key_conclusion": "Adaeze should approve only the modest pen set and reject the vacation because the FCPA's exception does not cover lavish personal benefits."
