      "source_id": "COSO IC 2013",
      "rule_or_proposition": "COSO IC 2013 Principle 8 requires the organization to consider the potential for fraud in assessing risks to the achievement of objectives, and fraud risk assessments conventionally apply the fraud triangle of pressure, opportunity, and rationalization.",
      "application_to_facts": "The coworker's mounting personal debt is a financial strain that creates motivation to commit fraud; it is the pressure element, distinct from his access to wire transfers (opportunity) or any excuse he might form (rationalization).",
      "key_conclusion": "The coworker's personal debt most directly represents pressure, the motivation component of the fraud triangle."
