    "ExplanationWrongC": "Silently reversing the entries conceals a control breakdown and leaves the flawed workflow in place; COSO IC 2013 requires the deficiency to be communicated and remediated, and the IMA Statement's Integrity standard bars concealing information relevant to the reliability of reported data.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Having the IT administrator who disabled the control review the affected postings recreates a segregation-of-duties failure; COSO IC 2013 requires independent review, so the person responsible for the change should not be the one validating the result.",
