    "ExplanationWrongC": "A certification shifts paperwork, not accountability; Competence requires the delegator to verify accuracy and understand limitations, and a signature cannot substitute for substantive review.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Review after guidance has already been issued cannot correct an inaccurate forecast that decision makers relied upon, so it fails the Competence duty to provide timely, accurate decision support.",
