    "Part2OnlyFlag": true,
    "UniqueConceptKey": "confidentiality-trade-secret-materials-database",
    "Stem": "Naomi Castellanos, project manager at Flash Industrial, oversees the proprietary materials-management database that contains the company's secret alloy formulation. A supplier Flash Industrial has worked with for years asks Naomi for the formulation details so it can tailor its services. Under the IMA Confidentiality standard, which statement describes Naomi's obligation?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Provide the details because the supplier is a long-trusted partner of the company.",
      "B": "Provide the details after the supplier signs a confidentiality agreement.",
      "C": "Refuse to disclose the formulation unless disclosure is authorized by the organization or required by law.",
      "D": "Share the formulation on Flash Industrial's internal portal so all teams can access it."
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "C",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "The IMA Confidentiality standard requires keeping information confidential except when disclosure is authorized by the organization or legally required; a trade secret cannot be shared without such authorization.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "Trust in a supplier does not constitute authorization to disclose a trade secret; the IMA Confidentiality standard bars disclosure of confidential information unless the organization authorizes it or law requires it, regardless of the recipient's relationship.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "A confidentiality agreement with the recipient does not authorize disclosure; only the organization's authorization or a legal requirement permits releasing confidential information, so an NDA cannot cure an unauthorized release of a trade secret.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Posting the formulation on an internal portal expands access well beyond those with a need to know and is not authorized disclosure; the Confidentiality standard requires safeguarding confidential information and monitoring its appropriate use.",
