    "UniqueConceptKey": "whistleblower-original-information-eligibility",
    "Stem": "Lena Fischer, a financial analyst at Flash Capital, discovers through her normal work that senior managers are booking fictitious revenue. She wants to report the fraud and is weighing eligibility for an award under the SEC whistleblower program, which builds on the whistleblower protections of SOX §806. Her colleague claims the only way to qualify is to get the story published first or to wait until the SEC opens an investigation. Under the SEC's rules, when is Lena's information considered original for award purposes?",
