    "ExplanationWrongC": "C wrongly treats proof of wrongful intent as a precondition for action; rationalization need not be admitted or proven before the controller acts, and limiting the response to an ethics acknowledgment leaves the quota pressure and the control weakness in place.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "D escalates the very pressure that drives the premature recognition; enlarging bonus incentives increases the incentive/pressure element rather than removing it, and it does nothing to correct the revenue already booked or to strengthen the cutoff controls.",
