    "Part2OnlyFlag": true,
    "UniqueConceptKey": "sox-302-certification-foreign-subsidiary-reliance",
    "Stem": "Adaeze Onuorah, CFO and certifying officer of Flash Holdings, must sign the quarterly certification under Section 302 of the Sarbanes-Oxley Act. Flash Holdings consolidates a foreign subsidiary whose books are prepared by local management and audited by a foreign firm, and Adaeze has not personally reviewed the subsidiary's underlying records. Adaeze asks whether relying on the subsidiary's management and auditor assurances is sufficient for her certification. Which analysis is most accurate?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Adaeze remains personally responsible for the certification covering the consolidated entity; reliance on subsidiary management or auditors does not relieve her of the duty to evaluate controls and disclosure controls",
      "B": "Adaeze may certify only Flash Holdings' parent-level statements and exclude the foreign subsidiary from the certification",
      "C": "The foreign auditor's opinion on the subsidiary is an acceptable substitute for Adaeze's certification duties",
      "D": "Adaeze's certification is valid if she relied in good faith on the subsidiary management's representations"
    },
