    "ExplanationWrongA": "Promotional intent does not justify omitting material unfavorable information; Regulation G prohibits presenting non-GAAP measures in a misleading way, and the Credibility standard requires fair and objective communication.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Non-GAAP measures are not inherently misleading; they are permitted when reconciled to GAAP and presented without obscuring material information, so avoiding them altogether is not the balanced approach.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Materiality does not depend on investor inquiry; the Credibility standard requires proactive disclosure of relevant information that could influence users' understanding, and Regulation G governs how non-GAAP measures are presented whenever they are used.",
