      "rule_or_proposition": "SAB 99 (Staff Accounting Bulletin No. 99) holds that materiality is a matter of professional judgment that cannot be reduced to a mechanical percentage test; both quantitative and qualitative factors must be considered, including whether the misstatement affects trends or how results are presented and communicated.",
      "application_to_facts": "The 0.3% misclassification is below the company's 5% quantitative threshold, but it changes the presentation of results and affects the trend of reported expenses, so a reasonable investor could regard the error as significant and Maya must apply professional judgment and disclose it.",
      "key_conclusion": "Maya must disclose the misclassification because materiality is a professional judgment that weighs qualitative factors such as trend presentation alongside quantitative size."
