    "UniqueConceptKey": "whistleblower-anonymous-channel-design",
    "Stem": "Mariela Hoffmann, the controller of Flash Manufacturing, is designing the company's confidential whistleblower channel before the year-end external audit. The audit committee has asked her to recommend a structure that encourages employees to report suspected fraud while complying with whistleblower protections. Which channel design best achieves that objective?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "An independently administered hotline and web portal that accept anonymous reports, prohibit retaliation, and escalate suspected fraud directly to the audit committee",
      "B": "A reporting process that routes every report through the employee's direct supervisor so the matter can be resolved at the lowest level of the organization",
      "C": "A channel that requires reporters to identify themselves so the compliance team can gather corroborating evidence before any investigation begins",
      "D": "A channel restricted to allegations of fraud above a $50,000 materiality threshold so the compliance team is not flooded with trivial complaints"
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "A",
