    "UniqueConceptKey": "ethics-of-budget-negotiation-pressure",
    "Stem": "During the annual budget negotiation at Flash Industrial, Adaeze Onuorah, the CFO, presses Mariela Hoffmann, the controller, to accept a revenue target that Hoffmann believes is unattainable so the company can present a more ambitious plan to the board. Hoffmann is considering several responses. Which response is most consistent with the IMA Statement of Ethical Professional Practice?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Accept the target because a budget is only an internal planning document that can be revised when actual results come in",
      "B": "Accept the target but quietly include an undisclosed cushion in the operating plan so the division can still be credited with meeting it",
      "C": "Decline to endorse the target, communicate her professional assessment of the assumptions to the CFO, and document the disagreement in writing",
      "D": "Accept the target and attribute the eventual shortfall to unfavorable market conditions that were beyond anyone's control"
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "C",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "The IMA Statement's Integrity and Credibility standards require communicating information fairly and objectively and disclosing all relevant information that could influence an intended user's understanding, so Hoffmann must state her disagreement rather than endorse an unattainable budget.",
