    "UniqueConceptKey": "internal-controls-fraud-prevention-role",
    "Stem": "Maya Caldwell, the risk officer at Flash Logistics, is explaining to the board how internal controls contribute to fraud prevention as the company prepares for its SOX §404 assessment. Which statement most accurately describes the role of internal control in preventing and detecting fraud?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "A well-designed system of internal controls ensures that fraudulent transactions will be detected promptly as they occur",
      "B": "Fraud prevention is primarily the responsibility of the internal audit function rather than operating management",
      "C": "The role of internal control is to detect fraud after it has occurred, because preventive controls cannot stop determined perpetrators",
      "D": "Internal control reduces the risk of fraud to an acceptable level but cannot eliminate it, because collusion and management override can defeat any control"
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "D",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "COSO IC 2013 defines internal control as providing reasonable assurance, not absolute assurance; because collusion and management override can defeat any control, even a strong control system cannot reduce fraud risk to zero.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "A control system cannot ensure the prompt detection of every fraudulent transaction; COSO IC 2013 is explicit that internal control provides reasonable, not absolute, assurance, and absolute-detection claims overstate what controls can achieve.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Under COSO IC 2013, operating management owns the design and operation of controls and sets the control environment; internal audit evaluates controls but does not carry the primary responsibility for preventing fraud.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "Preventive controls such as segregation of duties and authorization limits are a core element of COSO IC 2013 and deter fraud before it occurs, so internal control is not limited to detecting fraud after the fact.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "",
