    "Part2OnlyFlag": true,
    "UniqueConceptKey": "sustainability-disclosure-framework-selection",
    "Stem": "Priya Ramaswamy, the investor relations analyst at Flash Foods, is recommending a sustainability disclosure framework to the CFO. She is weighing SASB, which would report only climate metrics financially material to food processing; TCFD-aligned reporting, which would add Scope 1, 2, and 3 greenhouse gas emissions and climate-risk quantification; and GRI, which would cover the broadest set of material sustainability topics. Flash Foods currently discloses only Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions, measured at 40,000 and 10,000 metric tons per year, and estimates its upstream supply chain adds 150,000 metric tons of Scope 3 emissions annually. If Flash Foods adopts the TCFD-aligned framework and prices carbon at $50 per metric ton to quantify climate-related financial exposure, what additional annual exposure (in dollars) does the expanded Scope 3 disclosure newly reveal relative to the current Scope 1+2 disclosure?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "$7,500,000",
      "B": "$2,500,000",
      "C": "$10,000,000",
      "D": "$750,000"
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "A",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "The TCFD-aligned Scope 3 disclosure adds 150,000 metric tons at a $50 carbon price: 150,000 × $50 = $7,500,000 of newly revealed annual exposure. The current Scope 1+2 exposure (50,000 tons × $50 = $2,500,000) was already disclosed, so only the incremental Scope 3 amount is additional; the IMA Statement's credibility standard requires communicating that exposure fairly and objectively.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "$2,500,000 equals the already-disclosed Scope 1+2 exposure (40,000 + 10,000 = 50,000 tons × $50), so it represents what Flash Foods currently reports rather than the additional exposure created by adopting a TCFD-aligned Scope 3 disclosure.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "$10,000,000 is the total exposure across all three scopes (40,000 + 10,000 + 150,000 = 200,000 tons × $50); it overstates the newly revealed amount because the Scope 1+2 portion was already part of the company's existing disclosure.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "$750,000 results from misreading the Scope 3 estimate as 15,000 metric tons (15,000 × $50); the verified estimate of 150,000 metric tons produces an incremental exposure ten times larger.",
    "Difficulty": "Moderate",
    "DifficultyScore": 3,
