    "ExplanationWrongC": "C is wrong because whistleblower protection attaches to reasonable, good-faith reports and does not hinge on the investigation's outcome; SOX §806 protects employees whether or not the allegation is substantiated, and the reporter's identity should remain confidential even when the report is not confirmed.",
