    "UniqueConceptKey": "merger-negotiation-leak-escalation",
    "Stem": "Maya Caldwell, the risk officer at Flash Capital, discovers through routine surveillance that a colleague shared confidential terms of Flash Holdings' pending merger negotiations with an outside financial advisor who is not covered by a nondisclosure agreement, and the deal terms have begun to circulate. Maya is the only person besides the colleague who knows about the leak. Which of the following best describes what Maya should do under the IMA Confidentiality standard?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "Maya should take no further action because the information was already disclosed by someone else, and a confidentiality duty ends once confidential information has been released.",
      "B": "Maya should quietly delete the surveillance records to protect Flash Capital's reputation while the merger negotiations are still sensitive.",
      "C": "Maya should report the unauthorized disclosure through the appropriate internal channels and refrain from discussing the deal terms further, because the IMA Confidentiality standard requires keeping information confidential and the breach should be escalated before it harms the transaction or the market.",
      "D": "Maya should contact the outside advisor directly to warn him to stop discussing the deal terms, without notifying Flash Capital's legal or compliance functions."
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "C",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "The IMA Confidentiality standard requires keeping information confidential except when disclosure is authorized or legally required, so Maya should escalate the leak through proper internal channels and avoid further discussion of the deal terms.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "A is wrong because a confidentiality duty is not extinguished by another person's improper disclosure; the IMA Confidentiality standard still requires Maya to keep the information confidential and to escalate the unauthorized disclosure through proper channels rather than stand by while deal terms circulate.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "B is wrong because deleting surveillance records would conceal a compliance failure and potentially facilitate improper trading or further breaches of duty; the IMA standards require honest communication and escalation, and destroying evidence of the leak is itself misconduct that compounds the original breach.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "D is wrong because contacting the outside advisor directly could compromise the investigation, and the advisor's unauthorized receipt of confidential terms is a matter for Flash Capital's legal and compliance functions; Maya should escalate internally instead of managing the advisor herself.",
