    "ExplanationWrongD": "Choice D describes a proper presentation of the $1.1 million warranty provision with assumptions, but it does not identify the Credibility violation, which is the omission of the $600,000 reasonably possible contingency from the report. Presenting one disclosed item accurately does not make the report complete or fair when a relevant uncertainty that could influence the audit committee's decisions is withheld, so D cannot be the violating choice.",
