    "Topic": "F.446 fcpa-books-and-records-and-internal-controls",
    "Stem": "Flash Electronics analyst Adaeze Onuorah, CFO, is reviewing Flash's compliance after an audit found $45,000 in vague customs payments in Southeast Asia were recorded as miscellaneous operating expense without support for a $3 million shipment. Flash has $420 million revenue. Which FCPA books-and-records and internal controls requirement applies to the $45,000 entries?",
